; THE quirk. An unparseable posting line is not an error: it is skipped,
; and so is every posting after it in the same transaction. The transaction
; survives with fewer legs, which silently changes balances. `bean_core`'s
; loader carries a tripwire (`dropped_posting_warning`) precisely because of
; this. A rewrite that turns this into an error is a *better* parser, but it
; is a different parser — change this golden deliberately, not by accident.
2026-01-15 * "the second leg is unparseable"
  Expenses:Groceries  42.50 USD
  Assets:Bank:Checking  -42.50 US$
  Assets:Cash  0 USD

2026-01-16 * "everything after the bad line is gone too"
  Expenses:Groceries  1 USD
  not-an-account 1 USD
  Assets:Cash -1 USD
  Assets:Bank:Checking 0 USD

2026-01-17 * "a good transaction still parses after a mangled one"
  Expenses:Groceries  1 USD
  Assets:Cash        -1 USD
